  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zim_ReflectionEnumBackedCase_getBackingValue",
    "file": "php-src/ext/reflection/php_reflection.c",
    "description": "ReflectionEnumBackedCase::getBackingValue() attempts to resolve an IS_CONSTANT_AST case value with zval_update_constant_ex(), but ignores its FAILURE return. It then unconditionally treats ref->value as an enum object via Z_OBJ(ref->value) and passes it to zend_enum_fetch_case_value(). If evaluation failed, ref->value remains a constant AST/non-object zval and an exception is pending; interpreting its payload as zend_object causes the heap-buffer-overflow in zend_enum_fetch_case_value(). The method must return/propagate the exception when constant evaluation fails before accessing the enum object.",
    "conditions": "A backed enum case must have a backing-value constant expression whose deferred AST evaluation fails, and that case must be accessed through ReflectionEnumBackedCase::getBackingValue(). In the PoV, `enum Inm:int { case Foo=\\xff; }` produces such an unresolved/invalid constant expression; constructing `ReflectionEnumBackedCase(Inm::class, 'Foo')` retains the class constant, and getBackingValue() triggers failed AST resolution followed by the invalid object/property read."
  },
